.TH WAYPAPER 1 2026-08-30
.nh
.SH NAME
waypaper \- GUI wallpaper manager for Wayland and X11
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B waypaper
[ \fIOPTION\fR ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Waypaper
is a GUI wallpaper manager for Wayland and Xorg window managers, with support for gif and video wallpapers. It works as a frontend for popular wallpaper backends like swaybg, swww, awww, hyprpaper, mpvpaper, gslapper, feh, xwallpaper, wallutils, and linux-wallpaperengine.  \fIhttps://anufrievroman.gitbook.io/waypaper \fR
.SH OPTIONS

.TP
\fB\-v \fP, \fB\-\-version \fP
Print version.

.TP
\fB\-h \fP, \fB\-\-help \fP
Print help.

.TP
\fB\-\-restore \fP
Restore the last chosen wallpaper. Useful at launch of the window manager.

.TP
\fB\-\-random \fP
Set a random wallpaper.

.TP
\fB\-\-wallpaper XXX \fP
Set the wallpaper from the provided path and save it in the config.

.TP
\fB\-\-folder \fP
Set the folder of wallpaper images.

.TP
\fB\-\-monitor \fP
Set the desired monitor. Should be used together with either \-\-random or \-\-wallpaper.

.TP
\fB\-\-backend XXX \fP
Specify which backend to use, which can be either \fIswaybg, swww, awww, hyprpaper, mpvpaper, gslapper, feh, xwallpaper, wallutils, linux\-wallpaperengine\fR, or \fImacos\fR. Useful if you use waypaper on both Wayland and Xorg on the same machine. By default, last used backend is used.

.TP
\fB\-\-state\-file XXX \fP
Set the path to state file.

.TP
\fB\-\-config\-file XXX \fP
Set the path to configuration file.

.TP
\fB\-\-fill XXX \fP
Specifies filling type, which can be either \fIfill, stretch, fit, center\fR, or \fItile\fR.

.TP
\fB\-\-list \fP
List wallpapers, monitors, and backend in json format.

.TP
\fB\-\-no\-post\-command \fP
Prevent running the post command that was set in the config.

.TP
\fB\-\-zen\-mode \fP
Launch in Zen mode, which hides the top bar and options panel for a minimal, grid-only view.

.SH COMMANDS DURING USE
Press '\fB?\fP' during use to get a list of keybindings.
.br
